{:event/id "f6c89100-5760-4e83-8e89-8a3c26b23bdd" :event/schema {:schema/root "b91af160cb06543c10a8feafed4ae767cee20bd62e2e767d624d63065eee76f5" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:97bb851c-197d-4a07-a3b9-2db1a63e2168" :event/seq 1 :event/causes ["97bb851c-197d-4a07-a3b9-2db1a63e2168"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:97bb851c-197d-4a07-a3b9-2db1a63e2168" :event/at "2026-09-16T13:26:28Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/chat-rate-limit-is-availability-biased-admission-guard :finding/shapes #{:policy :gate :counter :failure-policy :infra} :finding/current-name "policy/check-rate-limit! + mongo-rate-limits/increment-rate-limit!" :finding/candidate-name "AvailabilityBiasedAdmissionGuard<Decision,Store>" :finding/claim "Chat rate enforcement composes the existing FixedWindowCounter with a separate admission failure policy: a successful count above maxRequests is rejected, while operational counter-store failures are deliberately swallowed. The tests codify that Mongo failure must not block chat. The counter law therefore does not determine permit/deny behavior when its storage capability is unavailable."}}
{:event/id "44cd620d-e23b-4759-aa36-10afd32e6d39" :event/schema {:schema/root "b91af160cb06543c10a8feafed4ae767cee20bd62e2e767d624d63065eee76f5" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:97bb851c-197d-4a07-a3b9-2db1a63e2168" :event/seq 2 :event/causes ["f6c89100-5760-4e83-8e89-8a3c26b23bdd"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:97bb851c-197d-4a07-a3b9-2db1a63e2168" :event/at "2026-09-16T13:26:28Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/github-ingestion-rate-limit-is-provider-directed-retry-budget :finding/shapes #{:retry :backoff :budget :protocol :infra} :finding/current-name "kms-ingestion.drivers.github/api-get + rate-limited? + retry-after-ms" :finding/candidate-name "ProviderDirectedRetryBudget<Response,Attempt>" :finding/claim "GitHub ingestion owns no local request-window counter. A 429 or qualifying 403 is provider evidence that authorizes another attempt; retry delay authority prefers Retry-After, then X-RateLimit-Reset, then exponential fallback. Attempts are bounded and each wait is capped, so this is a client-side retry budget under provider-owned quota state rather than FixedWindowCounter."}}
